# Spring Boot 2.7 to 3.2 Migration Guide

## Overview
Migrating from Spring Boot 2.7.x to 3.2.x is a major version upgrade requiring:
- Java version upgrade (minimum Java 11, recommended Java 21)
- Dependency updates
- Namespace migration (javax -> jakarta)
- API changes and deprecation handling

## Key Changes

### 1. pom.xml Parent Version
```xml
<!-- Before -->
<parent>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2.7.x</version>
</parent>

<!-- After -->
<parent>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
    <version>3.2.x</version>
</parent>
```

### 2. Java Version
```xml
<!-- Before -->
<java.version>1.8</java.version>
<maven.compiler.source>1.8</maven.compiler.source>
<maven.compiler.target>1.8</maven.compiler.target>

<!-- After -->
<java.version>21</java.version>
<maven.compiler.source>21</maven.compiler.source>
<maven.compiler.target>21</maven.compiler.target>
```

### 3. Common Dependency Updates
- Spring Cloud: Update to latest compatible version
- Database drivers: Update to latest versions
- Logging: Logback updated in Spring Boot 3.2
- JWT libraries: Keep compatible versions

## Migration Steps
1. Update parent version in pom.xml
2. Update Java version properties
3. Remove explicit dependency versions that are managed by Spring Boot
4. Update namespace imports (javax -> jakarta)
5. Handle deprecated APIs
6. Test thoroughly
