# RestTemplate to RestClient Migration

## Overview
Spring Boot 3.2 introduces RestClient as a modern replacement for RestTemplate. RestClient provides a fluent API and better error handling.

## Migration Examples

### 1. Basic GET Request
```java
// Before (RestTemplate)
RestTemplate restTemplate = new RestTemplate();
ResponseEntity<User> response = restTemplate.getForEntity(
    "http://api.example.com/users/{id}",
    User.class,
    userId
);
User user = response.getBody();

// After (RestClient)
RestClient restClient = RestClient.create();
User user = restClient.get()
    .uri("http://api.example.com/users/{id}", userId)
    .retrieve()
    .body(User.class);
```

### 2. POST Request with Body
```java
// Before (RestTemplate)
HttpEntity<CreateUserRequest> request = new HttpEntity<>(userRequest, headers);
ResponseEntity<User> response = restTemplate.postForEntity(
    "http://api.example.com/users",
    request,
    User.class
);

// After (RestClient)
User user = restClient.post()
    .uri("http://api.example.com/users")
    .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
    .body(userRequest)
    .retrieve()
    .body(User.class);
```

### 3. Error Handling
```java
// Before (RestTemplate)
try {
    User user = restTemplate.getForObject(url, User.class);
} catch (HttpClientErrorException e) {
    // Handle error
}

// After (RestClient)
User user = restClient.get()
    .uri(url)
    .retrieve()
    .onStatus(HttpStatusCode::isError, (request, response) -> {
        throw new RuntimeException("API Error: " + response.getStatusCode());
    })
    .body(User.class);
```

### 4. Bean Configuration
```java
@Configuration
public class RestClientConfig {
    @Bean
    public RestClient restClient() {
        return RestClient.create();
    }
}
```
